<h1>:x composite</h1>
<p>The 'single' value may be a composite or aggregate type. The idea is that all arguments must be prepared before any evaluation of the thread may take place.
Specifying 'one' value is useful so we can talk about aggregation separately.</p>
<h1>:x return</h1>
<p>Again, the return type may be composite.
A thread may also mutate a reference rather than explicitly returning a value, however the reference must be exclusive (like rust's mutable reference), write-only, or otherwise unable to affect the result after evaluation has begun.</p>
